.SH NAME
dotty-packages-edit - Open the profile's config.toml in the default editor.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdotty packages edit [--sync | --upgrade] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the profile's user-owned mise config.toml in $VISUAL / $EDITOR. The
component fragments under conf.d/ are re-rendered by dotty init and are not
the place for edits. With --sync or --upgrade, the corresponding command
runs after the editor exits.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for edit

.PP
\fB--sync\fP[=false]
	run \fBdotty packages sync\fR after editing

.PP
\fB--upgrade\fP[=false]
	run \fBdotty packages upgrade\fR after editing


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to operate on (defaults to the active profile)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  dotty packages edit
  dotty packages edit --sync
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBdotty-packages(1)\fP
